<!-- ============ LAKE IRIKI ============ -->
<section id="lake-iriki" class="sec">
  <div class="wrap igrid">
    <figure class="frame" data-rv="left"><img src="https://image.qwenlm.ai/public_source/59e3c0a3-0889-46ea-884f-ad206b7115d9/189a0c121-3a4e-4602-a90f-c87202965df4.png" alt="Mirage shimmering over the cracked earth of Lake Iriki with a nomad and camel" loading="lazy"></figure>
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow" data-rv>04 · The Mirage Plain</p>
      <h2 class="sec-title" data-rv>Lake Iriki</h2>
      <p class="mirage" data-rv>A lake that vanished — and never quite left.</p>
      <p class="body" data-rv>Once a true lake, Iriki is now a vast white plain where mirages pool on the horizon like water that refuses to be forgotten. Flamingos still return in rare wet years, and nomads cross its cracked mosaic with the ease of sailors on a calm sea.</p>
      <p class="body" data-rv>We drive it at golden hour, when the earth turns to porcelain and the sky performs. It is the finest natural stage in Morocco — and you will have the front row to yourself.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ ANTI ATLAS ============ -->
<section id="anti-atlas" class="sec">
  <div class="wrap agrid2">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow" data-rv>05 · The Ancient Bones</p>
      <h2 class="sec-title" data-rv>Anti-Atlas<br>Mountains</h2>
      <p class="body" data-rv>Older than the Alps, folded when the planet was young, the Anti-Atlas guards the road south in ochre and rust. Every bend is a gallery: fossil beds, volcanic necks, villages stacked like swallow nests.</p>
      <p class="body" data-rv>The drive from Agdz to Foum Zguid is, in our biased opinion, the most beautiful empty road in North Africa. We stop often. You will want to.</p>
      <ul class="tags" data-rv><li>Tizi n'Tichka alt. routes</li><li>Fossil beds</li><li>Kasbah valleys</li><li>Photographer's road</li></ul>
    </div>
    <figure class="tilt" data-rv="right"><img src="https://image.qwenlm.ai/public_source/59e3c0a3-0889-46ea-884f-ad206b7115d9/119baf062-68a8-4d81-9668-ecf1c55b51e7.png" alt="Winding road through ochre Anti-Atlas cliffs at evening light" loading="lazy"></figure>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ OASIS ============ -->
<section id="oasis" class="sec">
  <div class="wrap ogrid">
    <figure class="round" data-rv="scale"><img src="https://image.qwenlm.ai/public_source/59e3c0a3-0889-46ea-884f-ad206b7115d9/1b04ffae3-b583-42fe-9ba7-a02242514425.png" alt="Green date palm oasis with earthen house against Saharan dunes" loading="lazy"></figure>
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow" data-rv>06 · The Green Thread</p>
      <h2 class="sec-title" data-rv>Oasis Life</h2>
      <p class="body" data-rv>Where water surfaces, everything celebrates. Palms lean over mud walls, children race through irrigation channels, and the air smells of mint and wet earth. The oasis is the desert's love letter to itself.</p>
      <p class="body" data-rv>Walk the palmerie with a local farmer. Learn why a date palm is planted, married and buried like family. Taste fruit picked an arm's length from your hand.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

