  <div class="wrap ngrid">
    <figure class="nimg" data-rv="left"><img src="https://image.qwenlm.ai/public_source/59e3c0a3-0889-46ea-884f-ad206b7115d9/162a5aa2d-1f01-4784-aa50-16e6299de657.png" alt="Berber nomad in indigo turban pouring mint tea beside a campfire at dusk" loading="lazy"></figure>
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow" data-rv>07 · The Keepers of Silence</p>
      <h2 class="sec-title" data-rv>Nomad Culture</h2>
      <p class="body" data-rv>The nomads of the south never conquered the desert — they agreed with it. Their tents face the wind wisely; their hospitality is law. The first glass is bitter as life, the second strong as love, the third gentle as death. You will drink all three.</p>
      <p class="nquote" data-rv>"A guest is a gift of God. Even the enemy, once he enters the tent, is family until the sand covers his tracks."<b style="display:block;margin-top:10px;font:600 10px var(--sans);letter-spacing:.3em;color:var(--ember)">— SAHARAN HOSPITALITY CODE</b></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

